WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.992 --> 00:00:15.937
Zann and Darb out of the meeting.

2
00:00:16.277 --> 00:00:17.618
Perda and Gliss followed them.

3
00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:20.939
"What's wrong?"

4
00:00:21.159 --> 00:00:21.819
Gliss asked.

5
00:00:21.839 --> 00:00:25.101
"Darb, I figured you'd want to stay and find out more.

6
00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.522
Just think—soon you might have magic of your own!"

7
00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:32.364
"I'm not sure I want that," Darb said softly.

8
00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:37.825
"I mean, sometimes I think it might be nice to conjure my own food instead of asking someone

9
00:00:37.865 --> 00:00:38.585
else to do it.

10
00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:40.866
But "But what?"

11
00:00:41.206 --> 00:00:42.546
Gliss sounded perplexed.

12
00:00:42.566 --> 00:00:48.048
"All I want to do when I grow up is become an animal caretaker," Darb blurted out.

13
00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:50.389
"What if having magic gets in the way of that?"

14
00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:54.410
Now Zann understood why his friend looked conflicted.

15
00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.931
Most Voids were limited to a few simple jobs that required no magic.

16
00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:03.032
One of those jobs was animal caretaker.

17
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:06.597
Darb had dreamed of doing that for as long as Zann had known him.

18
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:09.559
"I understand," he told Darb.

19
00:01:09.579 --> 00:01:14.441
"But Magica will still need animal caretakers even if all the Voids get magic."

20
00:01:14.461 --> 00:01:17.142
"Maybe," Darb said.

21
00:01:17.162 --> 00:01:19.723
"But I'm used to being a Void.

22
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.744
I actually don't mind it."

23
00:01:22.824 --> 00:01:23.705
Zann was shocked.

24
00:01:24.265 --> 00:01:26.366
How could anyone not want magic?

25
00:01:27.466 --> 00:01:30.728
Still, Darb was his friend, so Zann didn't question him.

26
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.863
Instead he flashed a smile at Darb and changed the subject.

27
00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:38.145
"Do you think Laddno can really do what he's promising?"

28
00:01:38.165 --> 00:01:40.786
"I doubt it," Gliss said.

29
00:01:40.806 --> 00:01:44.409
"That guy says Laddno has some secret knowledge.

30
00:01:44.929 --> 00:01:47.791
But nobody knows for sure if the Source is real."

31
00:01:47.811 --> 00:01:52.614
"I read that it might be deep beneath Mount Mystery," Perda said.

32
00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:55.316
"Or maybe inside the Cave of the Unknown."

33
00:01:55.336 --> 00:02:00.900
"If the Source is in the Cave, then Laddno is out of luck," Zann pointed out.

34
00:02:01.652 --> 00:02:03.414
"The Cave was destroyed, remember?

35
00:02:04.555 --> 00:02:06.917
Let's get home before Boz starts to worry about us."

36
00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:12.603
When the kids reached Zann's house, a magical note was floating in the living room.

37
00:02:12.623 --> 00:02:15.425
"It's from Boz," Zann said.

38
00:02:15.445 --> 00:02:16.987
"Venna called another meeting.

39
00:02:17.427 --> 00:02:19.149
Boz won't be back for several hours."

40
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.671
Perda's eyes widened.

41
00:02:21.691 --> 00:02:24.374
"This is our chance to help Ello!"

42
00:02:25.555 --> 00:02:26.576
Zann swallowed.

43
00:02:27.168 --> 00:02:31.850
He knew Boz would be furious if he ever found out that the kids had gone out again.

44
00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:38.273
Zann quickly pushed that thought out of his mind and checked his pocket to make sure the guidelink

45
00:02:38.313 --> 00:02:39.193
was still there.

46
00:02:39.213 --> 00:02:41.054
"Let's go."

47
00:02:42.414 --> 00:02:43.595
They headed back outside.

48
00:02:44.095 --> 00:02:48.457
Zing tried to come with them, but Darb convinced the dragon to stay behind.

49
00:02:48.477 --> 00:02:51.358
"Maybe I should stay too."

50
00:02:51.778 --> 00:02:52.898
Gliss looked pale.

51
00:02:52.918 --> 00:02:56.300
"I swore I'd never go near a wormhole again!"

52
00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.601
"You'll be fine."

53
00:02:58.882 --> 00:03:00.003
Perda grabbed her hand.

54
00:03:00.023 --> 00:03:02.385
"Let's zap straight to Wormwood."

55
00:03:03.846 --> 00:03:06.008
Wormwood was as creepy as ever.

56
00:03:06.949 --> 00:03:13.194
A variety of makeshift huts huddled around the central green where a gnarled and ancient tree grew.

57
00:03:14.335 --> 00:03:19.660
The wormhole at the tree's base wasn't visible, but Zann remembered exactly where it was.

58
00:03:20.621 --> 00:03:23.664
On the way to the tree, they passed Wyssa's old hut.

59
00:03:24.776 --> 00:03:27.438
An older man with gray hair sat outside.

60
00:03:27.798 --> 00:03:30.099
He stared suspiciously as the kids went by.

61
00:03:30.899 --> 00:03:34.842
Suddenly there was a growl from the tent next door to Wyssa's hut.

62
00:03:35.722 --> 00:03:39.764
A small silver dragon leaped out, spitting shards of ice.

63
00:03:39.784 --> 00:03:42.145
"Eek!" Gliss cried.

64
00:03:42.165 --> 00:03:43.146
"Stay back!"

65
00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:48.409
"Sorry!" A young man hurried out of the tent and grabbed the dragon.

66
00:03:48.429 --> 00:03:49.589
"She won't hurt you."

67
00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:51.470
"Hey, it's you!"

68
00:03:51.671 --> 00:03:52.511
Perda blurted out.

69
00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:53.952
"The guy from the meeting."

70
00:03:55.412 --> 00:03:57.793
The man brushed his wild hair to the side.

71
00:03:57.813 --> 00:03:59.574
"Oh, were you there?"

72
00:03:59.894 --> 00:04:01.535
he asked in a friendly voice.

73
00:04:01.555 --> 00:04:04.876
"I hope you enjoyed it—especially you."

74
00:04:05.836 --> 00:04:06.937
He smiled at Darb.

75
00:04:06.957 --> 00:04:08.357
"You're a Void, aren't you?"

76
00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:10.538
"You live here?"

77
00:04:10.858 --> 00:04:12.659
Zann said before Darb could answer.

78
00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.840
He peered past the man.

79
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.901
Piles of strange items filled the tent.

80
00:04:18.862 --> 00:04:21.083
Other items lay in the grass outside the tent.

81
00:04:22.223 --> 00:04:24.124
"Yes, home sweet home."

82
00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.762
The young man noticed Zann's red hair and frowned.

83
00:04:28.643 --> 00:04:30.624
He turned back to Darb and Perda.

84
00:04:30.984 --> 00:04:31.985
"Some mess, hmm?

85
00:04:32.685 --> 00:04:34.487
I brought home a bunch of stuff from the meeting."

86
00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.348
"We should go."

87
00:04:36.548 --> 00:04:39.310
Gliss sounded nervous as she glanced toward the tree.

88
00:04:40.511 --> 00:04:41.451
The man ignored her.

89
00:04:41.471 --> 00:04:43.433
"Are you interested in joining our group?"

90
00:04:43.573 --> 00:04:44.433
he asked Darb.

91
00:04:44.453 --> 00:04:47.655
"We can use more help to get the word out about Void Rights."

92
00:04:48.796 --> 00:04:51.418
Zann expected Darb to mutter "no thanks."

93
00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:54.480
Instead Darb cleared his throat.

94
00:04:54.956 --> 00:04:57.537
"Did you say you brought back some things from the meeting?"

95
00:04:57.738 --> 00:04:58.078
he said.

96
00:04:58.098 --> 00:05:01.420
"I'd, uh, love to see that boat again."

97
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.161
"Of course!"

98
00:05:03.461 --> 00:05:04.401
the man exclaimed.

99
00:05:04.421 --> 00:05:07.923
"Our mission is to share new kinds of magic with everyone.

100
00:05:08.604 --> 00:05:10.345
Come in and look at it all you like."

101
00:05:10.365 --> 00:05:15.627
"Actually I was hoping to borrow the boat for a while," Darb said.

102
00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:16.868
"I'd like to study it."

103
00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:19.149
The man looked uncertain.

104
00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:20.730
"It's the only one we have.

105
00:05:21.391 --> 00:05:23.772
Laddno went to great personal trouble to acquire it."

106
00:05:24.832 --> 00:05:27.073
"I wouldn't need it for long," Darb added quickly.

107
00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:32.296
"I'd be happy to bring it back to Laddno campaign headquarters tomorrow to discuss how I can help

108
00:05:32.336 --> 00:05:32.856
the cause."

109
00:05:33.697 --> 00:05:35.338
The man still looked hesitant.

110
00:05:35.858 --> 00:05:37.339
But finally he smiled.

111
00:05:37.359 --> 00:05:38.900
"I suppose that would be all right."

112
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.222
Soon the deflated boat was draped over Darb's shoulders.

113
00:05:43.582 --> 00:05:45.123
The kids hurried toward the tree.

114
00:05:45.983 --> 00:05:47.024
"What was that all about?"

115
00:05:47.284 --> 00:05:47.965
Zann asked.

116
00:05:49.025 --> 00:05:50.666
Darb smiled slyly.

117
00:05:50.686 --> 00:05:52.227
"We're going to Skellia, right?

118
00:05:52.587 --> 00:05:54.068
A drowning world with weak magic?

119
00:05:54.496 --> 00:05:57.318
I thought a boat that doesn't require magic might come in handy."

120
00:05:57.338 --> 00:05:59.860
"Good thinking, Darb!"

121
00:06:00.121 --> 00:06:00.661
Perda said.

122
00:06:00.681 --> 00:06:03.924
"Now we won't have to use magic to create a raft."

123
00:06:03.944 --> 00:06:07.246
"And that means we won't attract the gulpers."

124
00:06:07.847 --> 00:06:12.991
Zann shivered, thinking of the magic-eating creatures that swam in Skellia's waters.

125
00:06:14.412 --> 00:06:18.496
When Zann and his friends approached the tree, the wormhole spun open.

126
00:06:18.516 --> 00:06:23.740
"I was hoping the wormhole had disappeared," Gliss joked weakly.

127
00:06:24.796 --> 00:06:26.397
"Not this one," Zann said.

128
00:06:26.417 --> 00:06:29.579
"It's been here for a long time."

129
00:06:29.619 --> 00:06:30.400
Perda laughed.

130
00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:37.284
"Hey, maybe the Source is located right here under this spooky old tree with its super powerful wormhole!"

131
00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.145
"Who knows?"

132
00:06:39.625 --> 00:06:41.066
Zann snapped his fingers.

133
00:06:41.766 --> 00:06:44.648
A Shackle spell linked the friends' hands together.

134
00:06:46.269 --> 00:06:48.150
Zann stepped toward the wormhole.

135
00:06:48.651 --> 00:06:49.131
"Let's go!"
